                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "MIDI lost is low-stakes \u2014 the loops keep playing, mappings just idle until the controller returns \u2014 so it surfaces as a transient toast in warning amber, not a persistent banner. This reverts the amber MIDI banner (the earlier spike) back to a toast. A toast is for an event; the audio-device-lost condition holds the screen because nothing is heard until it is fixed. See c\/device-lost for the full stakes principle."
              }
            ],
